<title>USA: Perdigao holders approve restructuring.</title>
<headline>Perdigao holders approve restructuring.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Perdigao SA Comercio e Industria said that its shareholders approved a restructuring that will allow the poultry and pork processor to take advantage of significant past tax losses carried forward.</p>
<p>Under the approved reorganization, the company's wholly owned subsidiaries, Perdigao Agroindustrial and Perdigao Avicola Rio Claro Ltda, will be merged into Perdigao SA Comercio e Industria.</p>
<p>The parent company will then create a new holding company and will be delisted from the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange. The holding company will then be the only publicly traded entity, Perdigao said.</p>
<p>Perdigao SA Comercio e Industria and the newly created Perdigao Holding will then be renamed Perdigao Agroindustrial SA and Perdigao SA, respectively.</p>
</text>
